<title>TURKEY: Turkey sees C/A gap $6.9 bln, trade gap $20.5 bln.</title>
<headline>Turkey sees C/A gap $6.9 bln, trade gap $20.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish Finance Minister Abdullatif Sener said on Monday he expects the 1996 current account deficit to rise to $6.9 billion from $2.3 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>He said the foreign trade deficit was expected to rise to $20.5 billion in 1996 from $14.1 billion in 1995.</p>
</text>
